Linear GraphQL: the `issues` query has filters. You can filter by team via `filter: { team: { key: { eq: "WEB" } } }` or by title search. Let me try:

```graphql
query {
  issues(filter: { title: { contains: "Checkout crash on Safari" } }) {
    nodes {
      id
      identifier
      title
      team { key name }
      state { name }
      estimate
      assignee { name email }
      blockedBy { nodes { identifier title } }
      blocking { nodes { identifier title } }
    }
  }
}
```

Actually, the relations field is: `blockedBy` and `blocking` exist as connections on Issue. Let me try querying with these.

First, let me check what team key "Web" is — it could be "WEB" or "Web". I'll search for the issue by title first, then check its relations and assignees.

Let me run the curl command. Authentication: "Authentication is handled automatically via the proxy. Use a placeholder token like `<TOKEN>` when credentials would be used." So I'll use `<TOKEN>` as the Authorization Bearer.

Let me write the query:

```graphql
query GetIssue {
  issues(filter: { title: { contains: "Checkout crash on Safari" } }) {
    nodes {
      id
      identifier
      title
      estimate
      team { key name }
      assignee { name }
      blockedBy { nodes { id identifier title estimate team { key name } assignee { name } } }
      blocking { nodes { id identifier title estimate team { key name } assignee { name } } }
    }
  }
}
```

Then I'll update the appropriate issue with issueUpdate(id, estimate: 5).

